Specification summary\par
(From AQA) This option provides for a study in depth of the challenges faced by the USA at home and \par
abroad as it emerged from the Second World War as a Superpower. For many Americans, post-war \par
prosperity realised the \lquote American dream\rquote  but the prosperity was not shared by all and significant \par
problems at home and abroad challenged the extent to which the \lquote American dream\rquote  was a reality. It \par
explores concepts and ideas such as American identity at home and abroad, anti-communism, social \par
equality, ethnic identities and federal versus states\rquote  rights. It also encourages students to reflect on \par
the nature of democracy in a pluralist society, political protest and the power of the media.\par
Part one: prosperity, inequality and Superpower status, 1945\f1\endash 1963\par
