Overview of US elections\par
The process to elect a president takes almost two years. Learn the steps that \par
result in the election of a U.S. president.\par
An election for president of the United States happens every four years on the \par
first Tuesday after the first Monday in November. The next presidential election \par
will be November 5, 2024.\par
What is the typical presidential election cycle?\par
The presidential election process follows a typical cycle:\par
Time of the year Event\par
Spring of the year before an election Candidates announce their intentions to \par
run.\par
Summer of the year before an election \par
through spring of the election year\par
Primary and caucus debates take \par
place.\par
January to June of election year States and parties hold primaries and \par
caucuses.\par
July to early September Parties hold nominating conventions to \par
choose their candidates.\par
September and October Candidates participate in presidential \par
debates.\par
Early November Election Day is the first Tuesday after \par
the first Monday.\par
December Electors cast their votes in the Electoral \par
College.\par
Early January of the next calendar year Congress counts the electoral votes.\par
January 20 Inauguration Day\par
