Long before he died at age 46, Kennedy was a very sick man.\par
As a child, Kennedy nearly died from scarlet fever and had serious \par
digestive problems which plagued him for the rest of his life. As a \par
young man, he suffered from urinary tract infections, prostatitis, \par
and a duodenal ulcer. Better known were his notorious spine and \par
back problems that began while playing football in college. His \par
lower back pain was so severe, he was initially rejected by both \par
the U.S. Army and the Navy when he first volunteered in World \par
War II.\par
In 1943 he led a heroic rescue of crew members of his patrol boat in the Pacific, \par
which involved swimming several miles while towing an injured man. The following \par
year, Kennedy underwent the first of four unsuccessful back surgeries; he had three \par
more between 1954 and 1957 while he was a U.S. senator. He was so ill at a few \par
points during this period that his Catholic priest administered last rites. Almost every \par
day of his adult life, he experienced debilitating back pain. Many times, his back was \par
so stiff from pain and arthritis that he could not even bend over to tie his shoes. Yet \par
Kennedy\rquote s most serious health issue was Addison\rquote s disease, an insufficiency of the \par
adrenal glands. If left untreated, it is life-threatening. The chronic use of steroids to \par
manage this likely caused osteoporosis of various bones in his body, most notably \par
his spine.\par
During his presidency, Kennedy was also treated with a slew of opiate pain killers, \par
local anaesthetic shots, tranquilisers, amphetamines and stimulants, including \par
Ritalin, thyroid hormones, barbiturate sleeping pills, gamma globulin to stave off \par
infections, as well as the steroid hormones he needed to keep his adrenal \par
insufficiency at bay. During the Cuban missile crisis he was prescribed increased \par
amounts of hydrocortisone and testosterone along with salt tablets to control his \par
adrenal insufficiency and boost his energy.\par
