DOMESTIC POLICY\par
The idea of the Great Society was introduced in two speeches in May 1964 and \par
developed in the 1965 State of the Union Address. What does it mean?\par
Johnson at Ohio University, 7 May 1964:\par
And with your courage and with your compassion and your desire, we will build a Great Society. It is a \par
society where no child will go unfed, and no youngster will go unschooled.\par
Johnson at the University of Michigan, 22 May 1964:\par
We are going to assemble the best thought and broadest knowledge from all over the world to find \par
these answers. I intend to establish working groups to prepare a series of conferences and \par
meetings\emdash on the cities, on natural beauty, on the quality of education, and on other emerging \par
challenges. From these studies, we will begin to set our course toward the Great Society.\par
State of the Union Address, 4 Jan 1965:\par
The Great Society asks not how much, but how good; not only how to create wealth but how to use it; \par
not only how fast we are going, but where we are headed. \'85 \par
I propose that we begin a program in education to ensure every American child the fullest \par
development of his mind and skills.\par
I propose that we begin a massive attack on crippling and killing diseases.\par
I propose that we launch a national effort to make the American city a better and a more stimulating \par
place to live.\par
I propose that we increase the beauty of America and end the poisoning of our rivers and the air that \par
we breathe.\par
I propose that we carry out a new program to develop regions of our country that are now suffering \par
from distress and depression.\par
I propose that we make new efforts to control and prevent crime and delinquency.\par
I propose that we eliminate every remaining obstacle to the right and the opportunity to vote.\par
I propose that we honor and support the achievements of thought and the creations of art.\par
I propose that we make an all-out campaign against waste and inefficiency.\par
Our basic task is threefold:\par
First, to keep our economy growing;\par
\emdash to open for all Americans the opportunity that is now enjoyed by most Americans;\par
\emdash and to improve the quality of life for all.\par
