war were made to a group of civilian employees who greeted \par
him at the Pentagon, where he went for a briefing on the \par
new United States military operations in Cambodia.\par
Mr. Nixon was cheered by public response to his television \par
speech on Cambodia last night. Ronald L. Ziegler, White \par
House press secretary, said telephone calls and telegrams received since Mr. Nixon \par
spoke were \ldblquote positive\rdblquote  in a ratio of six to one.\par
One such favorable comment came from a young woman in a group of Pentagon \par
